12. RO: Ce este o "secţiune critică"?
EN: What is a "critical section"?

A critical section is a section that must be protected by a mutex because more threads can reach the critical resources in that section simultaneously, changing their values in an unwanted and undifined way.

13. RO: Când aţi folosi un mutex în locul unui rwlock?
EN: When would you prefer using a mutex instead of a rwlock?

Rwlock allows multiple threads to access the resource, but only one to change it, while mutex allow only one reader and writer at the same time. I would use a mutex when only one thread needs to access the data at a time or when I have more writers than readers because it will avoid the overloads of mentaining separate reading and writing locks for readers and writers.

14. RO: Care va fi efectul înlocuirii apelurilor la pthread_mutex_lock cu apeluri la sem_wait?
EN: What will be the effect of replacing calls to pthread_mutex_lock with calls to sem_wait?

If we have a binary semaphore, it wont be any difference.
When we use pthread_mutex_lock, only the thread which initiated the lock can modify the critical resource protected by mutex, while sem_wait checks the value of the semaphore and if it is different than 0, it will allow to more threads to access the critical section and modify the value of the resource. If the value of the semaphore is 0, than no more threads are allowed to enter in the critical section until one spot becomes available.

15. RO: Ce face pthread_cond_wait cu mutex-ul primit ca argument?
EN: What does pthread_cond_wait do with the mutex it gets as argument?

pthread_cond_wait receives a locked mutex and automatically release the mutex, waiting for pthread_cond_signal or pthread_cond_broadcast which will "awake" the thread and the mutex will be unlocked before or after the signal was sent by the thread that reached the condition, then the pthread_cond_wait will lock the mutex again.

