20. RO: Explicaţi diferenţa dintre un link simbolic şi un link hard.
EN: Explain the difference between a symbolic link and a hard link.

A hardlink is another way to refer to the same file. It will create another name in the directory you are creating the link to, and refers it to the same inode number, that means that if you delete the initial file, the one you hard linked it will remain because it has a referrence to the inode and not to the initial file. When a hard link is created, the referrence counter of the inode is increasing and when you delete a file which refers to that inode, all the other files referring to the same inode will exist until the counter becomes 0.
A symbolic link is a file of a different type and it holds the path name of the linked-to file as the data of the link file and this time removing the original file, cause the link to point to a pathname that no longer exist.




